As I read the above, spe is the enchantment and spesgn is the sign 
of the enchantment.

     if(spe > rnd(5) && spe > otmp->spe) spe = 0;

I think rnd(5) gives you a number from 1-5 (but it might be 0-4, I don't
recall).  If the enchantment you ask for is greater than a random 
number from 1 to 5, you instead get a +0.

So, chances of getting what you ask for are:
+1   100%
+2   80%
+3   60%
+4   40%
+5   20%
>+5  0%

However, the following line is:
                if(spe > 2 && Luck < 0) spesgn = -1;

This means if you have negative luck, you won't get over +2.  If
you tend to get cursed -3 instead of blessed +3, your luck must be 
negative.  Perhaps when the moon is new, you might be better off 
wishing for just a +2.  Also, as David mentions, if you have 2 
blessed scrolls of enchant weapon, +2 is safer.

